      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e Note that this moves the call to rand::init() to before the logger has been initialized so we now must remember to not log from that function (or anything it calls), which sounds challenging to maintain.\n\nYes. I was considering moving the logger initialization to platform (which actually could be usefull for keeping x86_64 on higher logging verbosity temporarily), but I realized that rand init uses `panic!` for pontential logs 😅\n\n\u003e Could platform::init() be named `init_console()` and limited to that purpose? \n\n@mazurekm@google.com in the upcoming changes moves the extraction of FDT location to `platform::init()`. On aarch64 it\u0027s basically passthrough but on x86_64 it has to extracted from `boot_params`. So either the extaction has to refactored a bit or we leave the name. Honestly I am fine either way.\n\n\u003e Then, rust_entry() could even call `arch::rand::init()` directly, ensuring that as little code as possible runs with an uninitialized stack guard?\n\nSure, I can do that.",
